# AI Audit Log (CIC-307 NetArchitect)

Four places where AI-generated networking code was wrong. For each: the prompt, the
buggy code, the technical analysis (with packet-flow reasoning), and the fix that is
now in this repository. The "Observed output" blocks are the real output of running
the buggy snippet (`python3`), and each fix is locked in by a unit test.

| # | Area | Flaw | Fixed in | Regression test |
|---|------|------|----------|-----------------|
| 1 | Bitwise masks | `~mask` yields a negative Python int | `netarchitect/vlsm.py::wildcard_from_prefix` | `tests/test_vlsm.py::test_wildcard_masks`, `test_wildcard_never_negative` |
| 2 | VLSM sizing | Forgot network + broadcast (+2) | `netarchitect/vlsm.py::prefix_for_hosts` | `test_prefix_for_hosts_boundaries` |
| 3 | Optical budget | Ignored connector loss; one budget for every optic | `netarchitect/media.py` | `test_optical_budget_warning_and_margin`, `test_smf_beyond_400m` |
| 4 | Switchport trunks | Unconstrained trunk (all VLANs, native VLAN 1, DTP on) | `netarchitect/configs.py::_access/_core` | `test_configs_have_core_pieces` |

